WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.050
Avengers: Endgame is a love letter of a blockbuster,
paying tribute to the decade-plus of films

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:10.050
that came before it in inventive and exciting
ways; a true three-ring circus of Marvel mania,

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.540
full of characters from every part of the
MCU.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.820
Here's a breakdown of the characters with
more meaning than you may have realized.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.640
Endgame sees the surprising return of the
charismatic Frank Grillo as Brock Rumlow,

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:21.940
aka Crossbones.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.160
He appears in a new scene meant to take place
just moments after the conclusion of The Avengers'

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.780
Battle of New York, but before the whole team
clocks out to go and get shawarma.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.660
In his Endgame scene, Grillo is still a couple
years away from exposing himself as a HYDRA

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.390
lackey, still sporting his pretty face before
the events of The Winter Soldier left him

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.980
a burned-up, vengeful supervillain.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.120
While he was talked up as a main antagonist
of Civil War, his fate there was mostly to

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.200
be used as a hand grenade for Scarlet Witch.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.579
While he never reached his full potential
in the MCU, Crossbones is a recurring nemesis

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.020
for Captain America in Marvel Comics.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.380
But in the movies, he was promptly leapfrogged
and sidelined in favor of bigger and better

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.000
foes.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:02.580
Due to a number of complicated, business-related
reasons, Marvel Television and Marvel's movies

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.960
have never really been that closely-knit,
despite technically existing under the same

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.880
umbrella of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.940
With a few exceptions, the two worlds have
been kept very separate.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:14.180
If you have any doubts about this, ask someone
who's only watched the movies if they have

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.100
any idea what an Inhuman is supposed to be.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.740
It's a situation that makes the appearance
of Edwin Jarvis in Endgame all the more surprising.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.979
Edwin is the butler of Howard Stark and the
sidekick to Peggy Carter.

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:29.100
But unlike his co-lead, who was first introduced
in the movies, he's never before made an appearance

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.340
in the movies of the MCU.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.500
"Aren't you coming?"

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.400
"I thought I might sit this one out, actually."

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.220
While this is the character's first appearance
in an MCU movie, he was an integral part of

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.980
the TV series Agent Carter.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.759
Edwin is also obviously the namesake of Tony's
first A.I., Jarvis, whose voice was subsumed

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.960
into the Vision during the events of Age of
Ultron.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:51.260
While Agent Carter may not have set the world
on fire over the course of its two seasons,

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.660
it did develop a devoted following, and it's
not surprising that it's become the first

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.940
TV show to introduce a character that crossed
over into the movies.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:02.500
Not only did Kevin Feige have more involvement
with its development, it was created by Christopher

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.800
Markus and Stephen McFeely, the credited co-writers
of Endgame and Infinity War.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.580
While Iron Man's daughter may be an invention
of the movies, Scott Lang's daughter is anything

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.100
but.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:16.260
Scott meets up with Cassie after a five-year
time jump that, at the end of Endgame, appears

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.180
to be permanent.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:21.180
In the meantime, his precocious daughter has
grown up almost more than he can believe - but

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:24.830
if the comics are any indication of where
her story's going, she still has a lot of

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:25.700
development to go.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:30.100
In Marvel Comics, Cassie follows in her father's
footsteps in messing with the world of Pym

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.100
particles to give herself radical size-changing
powers, teaming up with her dad under the

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.610
names of Stature and Stinger.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.260
At times, she's as much of a partner to him
as the movies' Wasp is - and that's a relationship

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.520
we may get to see develop on screen as the
movies continue.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:47.340
While Endgame does in many ways feel like
a rare conclusive chapter in the MCU, producer

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:51.270
Kevin Feige has said that groundwork is being
laid for characters like Cassie to eventually

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.940
suit up as superheroes themselves.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:56.980
Speaking to Heroic Hollywood around the time
of Ant-Man and the Wasp's release in 2018,

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:59.790
Feige said,
"[We're] taking our cue from the comics as

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:04.440
we always do - that's why we wanted Cassie,
a very young Cassie in this movie, to be inspired

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.450
by her father.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.420
Just planting seeds."

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.380
Now here's someone who could've come in handy
in the fight against Thanos.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.610
In case you haven't seen Doctor Strange — or
just plain forgot about it — the Ancient

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:19.080
One is a character of major power and importance,
preceding Stephen Strange as the Earth's Sorcerer

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:19.600
Supreme.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.500
She shows up as the keeper of the Time Stone
in Greenwich Village's Sanctum Sanctorum during

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.440
the events of the Battle of New York, tracked
down by Professor Hulk in the hopes of getting

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.200
her to hand over her nice necklace.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.970
In addition to revealing that Marvel's Sorcerers
were indeed around to help out during the

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:36.870
Chitauri invasion, at least in their neighborhood
of New York City, Hulk's encounter with the

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:40.320
Ancient One reveals that she has always known
she would meet and be replaced by Stephen

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.880
Strange, who at the time of the Battle of
New York is still a practicing surgeon.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.660
Why she later claims in private conversation
not to want to train him during the events

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.900
of Doctor Strange is just one of many little
nitpicky inconsistencies that Endgame's time

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.500
travel story gives rise to, but considering
how nice it was to see this character again,

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.720
we can deal with a spare plot hole or two.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:03:59.860
"He reminds you of Kaecilius."

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:05.160
"I cannot lead another gifted student to power
only to lose him to the darkness."

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:10.080
It is possible that you were too distracted
by the sounds of weeping to really notice

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.840
who was attending the funeral of Tony Stark.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.460
The bittersweet affair reunited a number of
members of the MCU's deep bench, including

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:21.380
one slightly less-familiar face - a grown-up
version of Tony's potato-gun-shooting pseudo-sidekick

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.980
Harley, who last hung out with Tony during
his lowest moments of Iron Man 3.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.060
As the events of that movie detailed, Harley
is another kid with daddy issues whose family

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:33.470
life leaves something to be desired, much
like Tony Stark himself, or his other surrogate

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:34.490
son, Peter Parker.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:38.680
But Harley doesn't have the salve of a billion-dollar
fortune or some over-powered superhero skills

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.420
to take the edge off his shoddy home life.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.410
All he's got going for him is some witty Shane
Black dialogue and an admirable resilience

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:45.500
to Tony's savage put-downs.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:49.560
"Which happens, dads leave, no need to be
a p----- about it."

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.120
At the time of Iron Man 3's release, some
thought Harley might himself grow up to assume

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:55.300
some sort of Iron Man-adjacent mantle, a la
War Machine.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:58.820
While calls for that have pretty much faded
among the fanbase, it's still nice to see

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:02.900
an older version of the character pop up to
pay respects to the hero who was Iron Man.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.520
We wonder if he's getting anything from Tony's
will.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:10.200
Jasper Sitwell is, perhaps, nobody's favorite
character in the MCU, but he's been around

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.440
since nearly the beginning.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:16.260
In the MCU, Sitwell eventually reveals himself
to be on the HYDRA take - an allegiance which

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.600
was reflected in Endgame after the Battle
of New York.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:22.260
It just further hammers home the fact that
those HYDRA infiltrators were in S.H.I.E.L.D.'s

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.260
business for the long haul.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:27.070
In the comics, Jasper gets to remain a good
guy for the most part, only being manipulated

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:28.840
onto HYDRA's team for a brief while.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.080
Instead of being a bargain-bin bad guy that
most of the Avengers could deal with in a

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.140
single backhand, he's one of the most accomplished
agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.680
there is, serving as an interrogator for the
organization, a right hand man to Nick Fury,

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.160
and even taking over as director of the entire
organization for a time.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.920
In true Super Smash Bros. fashion, everyone
is there for the final battle of Endgame - minus

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.620
Black Widow and a cool pink robot, give or
take.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:54.240
But these absences are partially made up for
by the surprise appearance of Pepper Potts

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.770
suited up in her very own Iron Man-style armor.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:06:00.570
While she's certainly been in the thick of
the action before in the MCU, the CEO of Stark

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:04.280
Industries has never been as formidable a
player on the battlefield as she gets to be

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.040
in Endgame.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.680
Pepper's arrival into the fray this time isn't
some desperation move like the finale of Iron

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.840
Man 3, which saw her vaporize foes with the
help of some volatile Extremis serum and Tony's

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:14.180
repulsor ray gloves.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:18.500
Instead, she shows up in Endgame in a full
suit of Iron Man-style armor, designed especially

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.620
for her by Tony Stark.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:23.300
Sure, Pepper shows up to the fight as fan
service more than anything else.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:26.080
But she has an established a history as a
heroine in the comics, where she's known as

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:26.660
Rescue.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:30.260
Since she shows up to Endgame's last fight
with around 50,000 other fighters in tow,

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.420
it's hard to see how that name makes sense
in the movies.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:37.340
But it was still worth it for that instantly-iconic
back-to-back shot of husband and wife blasting

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:41.419
away at Thanos' minions together, working
together as a team for one last time before

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:41.960
the end.

